---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Kamil"
  description="Kamil Akin's path through borders, mathematics, startups, finance and storytelling."
>
  <header class="page-header container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
    <h1>A life between borders, numbers and stories.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I grew up crossing borders, literally. Now I am learning to turn those crossings into stories
      people can feel.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="about-grid container">
    <aside>
      <div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>KA</span>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Türkiye</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Work</dt><dd>Finance</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Study</dt><dd>Mathematics</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Current craft</dt><dd>Storytelling</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>

    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        I am the eldest child of an immigrant family and was raised in western Türkiye in a crowded
        home shaped by two citizenships and two cultures. My grandparents—the rockstars of our
        family—played a central role in raising me.
      </p>

      <p>
        Before I turned eighteen, I crossed international borders more than one hundred times. Moving
        repeatedly between countries and cultures taught me that the same place, event, or person can
        look completely different depending on where you stand.
      </p>

      <h2>A non-linear education</h2>

      <p>
        Numbers became another language for me. I answered every mathematics question correctly in
        the national university entrance examination and chose to study mathematics. From the outside,
        that might sound like the beginning of a predictable academic path.
      </p>

      <p>It was not.</p>

      <p>
        I left and returned to university more than once. During my undergraduate years, I attempted
        several startups; none became the success I imagined. Eventually, I completed my mathematics
        degree and began a master's program—then left during its second month.
      </p>

      <p>
        Today, I work in finance and spend some of my free time supporting founders through startup
        acceleration. Finance gives me structure. Startups keep me close to experimentation. Failure
        taught me to begin again.
      </p>

      <h2>Why storytelling?</h2>

      <p>
        I do not want merely to speak clearly. I want to understand why some stories disappear when a
        speech ends while others remain with us for years.
      </p>

      <p>
        Storytelling is where the different parts of my life begin to meet: the child crossing
        borders, the mathematics student attracted to structure, the founder who experienced failure,
        the finance professional who values clarity, and the speaker learning to transform experience
        into meaning.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        My goal is not only to reach a stage. It is to become a storyteller worth listening to.
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        My current goal is to compete in the Toastmasters national speech contest in Türkiye. Reaching
        that stage is not guaranteed. This diary records the maps, lessons, mistakes, feedback, and
        rewrites along the way—without publishing my complete final contest speech.
      </p>

      <p><a class="button" href={`${base}diary/`}>Follow the diary</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding-block: 6rem 4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 8vw, 6.8rem);
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 46rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 16rem minmax(0, 43rem);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 9rem);
    padding-top: 5rem;
  }

  .portrait {
    display: grid;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    place-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--surface);
    background: var(--accent);
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 4rem;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
  }

  dl div {
    padding: 0.8rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    aside {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .portrait {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
